## ESP32 Boot Spike — Headless test script
## Validates ESP32 platform definition, CPU execution, and UART output.
##
## Usage:
##   cd /path/to/Meadow.OS.Emulator
##   mono /Applications/Renode.app/Contents/MacOS/bin/Renode.exe --console --disable-xwt \
##     -e 'include @scripts/esp32-boot-test-headless.resc; start; sleep 2; cpu PC; quit'
##
## Expected output:
##   - 35 "read from empty FIFO" warnings (= "Hello from ESP32 Xtensa on Renode!\n")
##   - CPU PC should end at 0x40080050 (spin loop after UART output)
##
## What this validates:
##   1. meadow-esp32.repl loads correctly (all memory regions + peripheral stubs)
##   2. Xtensa CPU with esp32 cpuType executes windowed-ABI code
##   3. ESP32_UART receives data from CPU-executed code

using sysbus

# Create the ESP32 machine
mach create "esp32"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/meadow-esp32.repl

# Set up UART terminal on port 4245
emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal 4245 "esp32uart" false
connector Connect uart0 esp32uart

# Load bare-metal hello-world ELF (built with xtensa-esp32-elf-gcc)
sysbus LoadELF @tests/esp32-hello/esp32-hello.elf

# Set PC to _start (after literal pool)
cpu PC 0x40080010

log "ESP32 boot spike ready. Use 'start' to run."
